PAR-58 "Windows consumer for the shared Lua contracts" (docs/ERGOPTIPLUS_TODO.md): about 105 shared contracts (~940 cases) under static/ergopti_plus/_shared are consumed by the Linux and macOS runners but not by the Windows AutoHotkey suite. Build the Windows consumer as the entry describes, contract family by contract family, one atomic commit per family. AutoHotkey v2 runs under Wine in this container: reuse the setup from `origin/agent/windows-ahk-wine` (fetch it) or install wine64 + AutoHotkey v2 portable yourself. Execute what you add under Wine; list what could not run.
